{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "agent-session-orchestration",
  "title": "Long-lived Agent Session Orchestration",
  "description": "How the platform runs long-lived AI agent sessions through a shared control plane.\n\n**Top row (request path, left to right):** Client app → API Tier (open session, authenticate, resolve workspace and quotas) → Session Scheduler (select runner host under residency/isolation rules and the capacity pool) → Runner Host, whose Orchestrator Turn Loop assembles a request, calls the model, executes tool calls (idempotency keys toward external systems), appends results and checks for finish/ceiling before the next turn.\n\n**Second row:** Recovery and Lifecycle (heartbeat monitor, rescue from checkpoint, idle/suspend releasing runners, resume-and-rehydrate on any host, plus a Cancellation subsection that stops the stream, abandons tools, records uncertain outcomes and commits a resumable checkpoint); Durable State (Event Log feeding metering, cost and forensic replay; Snapshot Chain of content-addressed checkpoints with forks and reachability GC); Session Tree and Quotas (spawn child with scoped context and budget, child result back to the parent, orphan reaper, tree/workspace quotas pausing for a user decision); Release Drain (old-version host stops placements and drains sessions via completion, suspension or safe checkpoint before replacement).\n\nColor key: blue request path, violet agent execution, green durable state, orange quotas/budget, teal lifecycle/recovery, red failure/cancellation.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
